  "text_sample": "Your Page Title aubergine projects menu aubergine close Services Projects Garden care About Areas Journal Free quote Overview +34 960 000 000 [email protected] Cam\u00ed de Vera 18, 46022 Valencia 21 May 2026 A lawn that survives August Meadow mixes of native grasses and wild flowers, mown four times a year and watered almost never. Written by Ingrid Halvorsen Topic Planting Reading 1 min A green lawn in Valencia in August costs around 2,000 litres of water per square metre a year. Most of the lawns we replace were watered every evening and still turned the colour of straw by the end of July. There are two honest alternatives, and which one fits depends on how the space is used. For walking on: a tough mix Where children play or a dog runs, we sow a mix based on bermuda grass and zoysia. Both go golden in the heat and green again with the first September rain. Mown high and watered deeply once a week, they use about a third of the water of a classic lawn. For looking at: a meadow Where the grass is mostly seen, from a terrace or along a path, we sow a meadow. Our mix has 24 native species: grasses like brachypodium and stipa, and flowers like poppy, cornflower, wild marigold and viper\u2019s",
